{
  "abstract": "The coherent J/$\u03c8$ photoproduction cross section is measured for the first time at midrapidity in peripheral to semicentral Pb$-$Pb collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{\\rm NN}} = 5.02$ TeV. The centrality differential cross section ${\\rm d} \u03c3/ {\\rm d}y$ is reported for the centrality range 40-90%, together with the doubly-differential cross section ${\\rm d}^2 \u03c3/{\\rm d}y {\\rm d} p_{\\rm T}$, extracted in two peripheral centrality classes. The J/$\u03c8$ mesons are reconstructed in the dielectron channel, in the rapidity interval $|y| < 0.9$ using the ALICE central barrel detectors. The J/$\u03c8$ cross section at midrapidity is statistically compatible to the earlier ALICE measurement at forward rapidity and at the same centre-of-mass energy, and shows only a mild centrality dependence over the covered range. Several sets of theoretical calculations taking into account the hadronic overlap in the collisions but ignoring possible final-state effects from a hot expanding medium are found to give a fairly good description of the current measurements within uncertainties.",
